        "content": "{\"answer_text\":\"The financial guide (ASIC RG 271) says firms should consider a broad range of possible remedies when attempting to resolve complaints, including an explanation of the circumstances, an apology, assistance and support, a refund or waiver of a fee or charge, a goodwill payment, compensation, waiver of a debt, correcting records, changing contract terms, ceasing legal or other action that may cause detriment, and undertaking improvements to systems, procedures or products. It also says firms should ensure agreed resolution outcomes are implemented in a timely manner when a complaint is closed.\\n\\nThe workplace guide (Fair Work “Effective dispute resolution best practice guide”) describes dispute outcomes in terms of process goals: it promotes fairness and says a good dispute resolution process reassures employees they are being heard, sets expectations, establishes an escalation process if the dispute can’t be resolved by discussion, and aims for prompt and transparent resolution (including that employees know the steps and potential outcomes).\",\"citations\":[\"asic_rg271-p0043-c001-530991c66702\",\"fwo_dispute_resolution-p0008-c002-dec9ca7c9c5d\"],\"confidence\":0.74,\"output_type\":\"ANSWER\"}",
